From 4de8288c69df6acb8c1b587b40f6537da8598d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SpicyEggSalad <177426835+SpicyEggSalad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] gpu: read back 16 bit targets in their own format, at
 console size

Read-backs assumed 32 bit surfaces: a 16 bit render target (R5G6B5,
A1R5G5B5, X1R5G5B5, A4R4G4B4) was refused as too small, so the title
read nothing back. Sims 2 paints easel pictures this way and every
painting but one came out black. Targets now carry the guest surface's
format, pitch and bytes a pixel, and Sync and DeliverLate pack the
pixels into it, in both backends.

Such a surface is drawn to be read back, often colour keyed: Sims 2's
self portrait clears to a key colour and turns exactly-key pixels into
background. At render scale the read-back shrink blended the edges into
the key and left a pink fringe, so these targets and the depth drawn
with them are now made at the console's size.

Captures also list each stage's filter and address modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
